## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates comprehensive system design skills for building a scalable, multi-region, multi-tenant telemetry pipeline with strict isolation requirements using AWS serverless primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant Kinesis partitioning strategies for data isolation
- Idempotent event processing with DynamoDB deduplication
- Schema evolution management via Glue Catalog integration
- 7-day backfill implementation and fault tolerance patterns
- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry tracing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: Idempotent deduplication framework
function processEvent(event) {
  const compositeKey = `${event.tenantId}|${event.deviceId}|${event.timestamp}`;

  // Check for existing record to ensure idempotency
  const existingRecord = await dynamoDB.getItem({
    Key: { id: compositeKey }
  });

  if (!existingRecord.Item) {
    // Process and store new event
    await storeEvent(event);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests handling of cross-region, multi-tenant telemetry with data quality gates and runtime policy enforcement, requiring the candidate to design a robust data lineage, idempotence, and schema evolution using DVA primitives.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant isolation with Kinesis Streams and DynamoDB catalog
- Glue Schema Registry for backward/forward compatibility
- Runtime data quality checks and DLQ handling
- Idempotent writes and cross-region S3 replication
- OpenTelemetry tracing across services

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent write to DynamoDB
async function idempotentWrite(event, db) {
  const key = event.deviceId + '|' + event.ts;
  await db.put({
    TableName: 'idempotency',
    Item: { key, ts: event.ts },
    ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(key)'
  }).promise();
  return true;
}
```

